<title>USA: US lawmakers urge SEC investigation on arbitration.</title>
<headline>US lawmakers urge SEC investigation on arbitration.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three U.S. legislators criticized the use of mandatory arbitration in employment discrimination and sexual harrassment cases and urged the Securities and Exchange Commission to investigate  the practice.</p>
<p>Rep. Edward Markey of Massachusetts, Rep. Anna Eshoo of California and Rep. Jesse Jackson Jr of Illinois, all Democrats, asked the SEC to look into self-regulatory organizations that oversee the activites of securities firms and allow the continued use of mandatory arbitration in such cases.</p>
<p>((--Aaron Pressman 202-898-8312))</p>
</text>
